<title>UK: Country Casuals up, report raises bid hope.</title>
<headline>Country Casuals up, report raises bid hope.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Country Casuals Holdings Plc leapt on Monday after a report in the Mail on Sunday newspaper said Alexon Plc was poised to make a bid for the women's fashion retailer, dealers said.</p>
<p>Country Casual shares jumped 10-1/2p to 130p by 0837 GMT in light volume of 11,000 shares. while Alexon eased half a penny to 200p.</p>
</text>
